<header><p class="enc-kicker">State</p><h1 class="enc-title">Isin dynasty</h1><p class="enc-meta">Also known as Isin and Larsa dynasties</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Isin dynasty was a line of kings who ruled from the city of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/isin">Isin</a> in southern <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mesopotamia">Mesopotamia</a> after the collapse of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/third-dynasty-of-ur">Third Dynasty of Ur</a>. It claimed continuity with <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ur">Ur</a>'s rulers and competed with the dynasty of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/larsa">Larsa</a>. Its rise marks the fragmentation that followed the end of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/neo-sumerian-empire">Neo-Sumerian Empire</a>.</p></div>
